{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he saw the place from afar.</b> But not from close by — for he saw the radiance of the Shechinah of the Holy One, blessed be He, which is called 'the Place of the world,' specifically from afar: a sensory seeing like gazing at the sun, for from afar a person can gaze at it, but not from close by, for the faculty of sight has no power to gaze at the sun when it is close to a person. All the more so, by a fortiori from the fortiori's grandchild — the radiance of the splendor of His Shechinah, blessed be He. And so Moses said (Exodus 3:3), ״אָסוּרָה נָּא וְאֶרְאֶה״ and so forth — ״אָסוּרָה נָּא״ means to move away from the holy place and not be close to it, and all this in order that he might be able to see. And so Jeremiah said (Jeremiah 31:2), ״מֵרָחוֹק ה׳ נִרְאָה לִי״ — meaning, but not from close by."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:57.700727823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}